---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import CaseStudy from '../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
import CaseStudyHero from '../../components/CaseStudyHero.astro';
import StatCards from '../../components/StatCards.astro';
import MoreCaseStudies from '../../components/MoreCaseStudies.astro';
import BrowserFrame from '../../components/BrowserFrame.astro';
import Lightbox from '../../components/Lightbox.astro';

import heroImg from '../../assets/work/pensaar/hero.jpg';
import workImg from '../../assets/work/pensaar/work.jpg';
import servicesImg from '../../assets/work/pensaar/services.jpg';
import aboutImg from '../../assets/work/pensaar/about.jpg';

const stats = [
  { num: '25%', label: 'Increase in lead conversion rate' },
  { num: '65%', label: 'Boost in mobile engagement' },
  { num: '40%', label: 'Increase in average session duration' },
];
---

<CaseStudy
  title="Pensaar Design · Elevating a Design Agency's Web Presence"
  description="Redesigned and rebuilt Pensaar Design's website, migrating off a restrictive Squarespace template and reconstructing it in Wix, with an information architecture that matches how the agency wants to be understood."
>
  <CaseStudyHero
    title="Elevating the Digital Presence of a Design Thinking Agency"
    lead="I redesigned and rebuilt Pensaar Design's website, moving it off a restrictive Squarespace template and reconstructing it in Wix, with an information architecture that finally matched how the agency wanted to be understood."
    tags={['Web Redesign', 'CMS Migration', 'Internship · 2020']}
    meta={[
      { key: 'Role', val: 'Service Design Intern' },
      { key: 'Client', val: 'Pensaar Design' },
      { key: 'Platform', val: 'Squarespace → Wix' },
      { key: 'Timeline', val: '6 weeks' },
    ]}
    heroPlaceholder="Pensaar Design website"
  >
    <Image slot="hero-image" src={heroImg} alt="Pensaar Design redesigned website homepage" class="cs-hero-img-el" loading="eager" />
  </CaseStudyHero>

  <div class="cs-body">
    <div class="container">

      <!-- Context note -->
      <div class="cs-section" style="padding-top:0;">
        <blockquote class="cs-insight reveal" style="margin:0;">
          <p>An early-career project, from before I joined TCS. I interned at Pensaar Design in Bengaluru in 2020 as a service design intern, and this website redesign was part of that work. I've kept it in the portfolio because its core lesson, that the structure of a site shapes trust before the visuals do, still holds up in the enterprise work I do now.</p>
        </blockquote>
      </div>

      <!-- Problem / Solution -->
      <div class="cs-section">
        <div class="cs-two">
          <div class="reveal">
            <span class="cs-section-lbl">Problem</span>
            <h2 class="cs-subheading">The platform was undermining the agency it was meant to represent</h2>
            <p class="t-body" style="margin-top:1rem;">Pensaar Design's existing Squarespace website constrained their ability to showcase UX expertise. The template-driven platform limited how they displayed complex case studies, featured an outdated visual identity, and made it difficult for potential enterprise clients to navigate their services or understand their design philosophy.</p>
            <p class="t-body" style="margin-top:.75rem;">The core tension: an agency selling human-centred design was using a tool that prioritised the template's constraints over the agency's communication needs.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="reveal" style="transition-delay:.1s;">
            <span class="cs-section-lbl">Solution</span>
            <h2 class="cs-subheading">A site built to showcase the work, not just describe it</h2>
            <p class="t-body" style="margin-top:1rem;">I redesigned the site and rebuilt it in Wix, hand-constructing every page, the navigation, and the responsive behaviour inside the platform. The new site introduced a more premium aesthetic, a navigation anchored to a clear discovery journey, and proper in-depth sections for case studies and methodology.</p>
            <p class="t-body" style="margin-top:.75rem;">Delivering inside the CMS, rather than handing off a design file, meant the agency was left with a site their own team could run and update without a developer.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Design Process -->
      <div class="cs-section">
        <span class="cs-section-lbl">Information Architecture &amp; Visual Design</span>
        <h2 class="cs-heading reveal">Designing the <em>discovery journey</em> for a consulting client</h2>

        <!-- IA before / after -->
        <div class="reveal" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
          <p class="t-body" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;max-width:62ch;">
            The single highest-impact change was the order of the navigation. The structure, not the visuals:
          </p>
          <div class="ia-flow">
            <div class="ia-row">
              <span class="ia-row-tag is-before">Before</span>
              <div class="ia-chips">
                <span class="ia-chip">Services</span>
                <span class="ia-sep" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                <span class="ia-chip">Case studies</span>
                <span class="ia-sep" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                <span class="ia-chip">Philosophy</span>
              </div>
              <p class="ia-note">Pitch first. Buyers had to trust a price list before they understood the thinking behind it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="ia-row">
              <span class="ia-row-tag is-after">After</span>
              <div class="ia-chips">
                <span class="ia-chip is-active">Design philosophy</span>
                <span class="ia-sep" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                <span class="ia-chip is-active">Case studies</span>
                <span class="ia-sep" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                <span class="ia-chip is-active">Services</span>
              </div>
              <p class="ia-note">Thinking first. It mirrors how enterprise buyers actually evaluate an agency: who you are, what you believe, what you've done, what you offer.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cs-grid-3" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
          <figure class="cs-figure reveal" style="margin:0;">
            <BrowserFrame label="Work · By industry">
              <Image src={workImg} alt="Pensaar Design work page organised by industry" data-lightbox loading="lazy" />
            </BrowserFrame>
            <figcaption class="cs-figure-cap">Work: case studies, surfaced before the service list</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="cs-figure reveal" style="margin:0;transition-delay:.08s;">
            <BrowserFrame label="Services">
              <Image src={servicesImg} alt="Pensaar Design services page" data-lightbox loading="lazy" />
            </BrowserFrame>
            <figcaption class="cs-figure-cap">Services: what they offer, once the thinking is established</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="cs-figure reveal" style="margin:0;transition-delay:.16s;">
            <BrowserFrame label="About Us">
              <Image src={aboutImg} alt="Pensaar Design about page" data-lightbox loading="lazy" />
            </BrowserFrame>
            <figcaption class="cs-figure-cap">About: the agency's philosophy, leading the discovery journey</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Impact -->
      <div class="cs-section">
        <span class="cs-section-lbl">Business impact</span>
        <h2 class="cs-heading reveal">A platform that works as hard as the agency does</h2>
        <p class="t-body cs-intro reveal" style="transition-delay:.08s;">
          The redesign gave Pensaar a site that worked for them rather than against them. Better structure and properly-presented case studies meant enterprise clients could follow the discovery journey as intended — and the metrics confirmed the navigation change was the right call.
        </p>
        <StatCards stats={stats} />
      </div>

      <!-- Learnings -->
      <div class="cs-section">
        <span class="cs-section-lbl">Learnings &amp; Reflections</span>
        <h2 class="cs-heading reveal">What this project taught me</h2>
        <div class="cs-two" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
          <div class="reveal">
            <p class="t-body">This project was a useful reminder that information architecture decisions are often more impactful than visual ones. The biggest improvement to the site came from restructuring the navigation, not from the visual redesign. Enterprise buyers evaluate an agency in a specific sequence: who are you, what do you believe, what have you done, what do you offer. The previous site inverted that order.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="reveal" style="transition-delay:.1s;">
            <p class="t-body">Six weeks is a compressed timeline for a full redesign and migration. On a project like this I'd push for at least one round of user testing with prospective clients before launch. We validated with stakeholders, not with actual buyers, which is a gap. The conversion-rate improvement suggests the architecture change worked, but we don't know what we may have left on the table.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  <MoreCaseStudies current="pensaar" />
  <Lightbox />
</CaseStudy>

<style>
.ia-flow {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 1rem;
}
.ia-row {
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 2px;
  padding: 1.5rem 1.6rem;
}
.ia-row-tag {
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: .58rem;
  letter-spacing: .12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  display: inline-block;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}
.ia-row-tag.is-before { color: var(--text-3); }
.ia-row-tag.is-after { color: var(--accent); }
.ia-chips {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: .65rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.ia-chip {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: 1.05rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--text-3);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 2px;
  padding: .45rem .9rem;
}
.ia-chip.is-active {
  color: var(--text-1);
  border-color: rgba(201,169,110,.4);
  background: var(--accent-bg);
}
.ia-sep { color: var(--text-3); font-size: .85rem; }
.ia-note {
  font-size: .8rem;
  line-height: 1.6;
  color: var(--text-2);
  margin-top: 1rem;
  max-width: 64ch;
}
:global([data-theme="light"]) .ia-chip.is-active { border-color: rgba(154,110,42,.4); }
@media (max-width: 540px) {
  .ia-sep { display: none; }
  .ia-chips { gap: .5rem; }
  .ia-chip { flex: 1 1 100%; text-align: center; }
}
</style>
